            <ArticleTitle>[Anterior interosseus nerve syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5192-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A prolonged period of illness in a patient showing symptoms of reflexdystrophy is described. After going through several examinations and finally being referred to a pain clinic the patient demanded a second opinion from an orthopaedic surgeon. Her symptoms turned out to have been caused by a compression syndrome of the anterior interosseus nerve.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
